messages:
Jamie D: Heads up — I opened a docs PR to clarify how union types + arrays should be represented in structured output for function/tool calling. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/482. Need a quick review and two concrete snippets (JS+Python) that show the recommended envelope vs the unwrapped array pattern.

Priya R: Nice, thanks. Can you summarize the breaking case we ran into? I remember something about ambiguous parsers when the top-level value is a raw array. :thinking_face:

Jamie D: tl;dr: if the model returns an unwrapped array as the top-level response (e.g., `[ {"type":"text"}, {"type":"image"} ]`), some tool-caller parsers assume that means "call the tool for each element" vs "this is a single payload with an array field". Envelope avoids that: `\{"output_type\":\"batch\", \"items\": [...] \}` — explicit discriminator.

Alex K: putting an example here to use in the PR. Use the two forms and show how a simple schema validator distinguishes them.

```json
// Envelope (recommended)
{
  "output_type": "batch",
  "items": [
    { "kind": "text", "text": "OK" },
    { "kind": "image", "url": "https://example.com/1.png" }
  ]
}

// Unwrapped array (ambiguous)
[
  { "kind": "text", "text": "OK" },
  { "kind": "image", "url": "https://example.com/1.png" }
]
```

Alex K: For the schema, something like: `oneOf: [ { type: object, properties: { output_type: { const: 'batch' } } }, { type: array } ]` so validators can flag arrays that aren't wrapped.

Eli M: For SDK snippets — propose a tiny TS helper to normalize the response into the envelope shape (server-side). Example:```ts
export function normalizeOutput(res: any){
  if (Array.isArray(res)) return { output_type: 'batch', items: res };
  return res;
}
```

Eli M: And a python version to add to the samples:```py
def normalize_output(res):
    if isinstance(res, list):
        return {"output_type": "batch", "items": res}
    return res
```

Priya R: Those look good. Can we also add a short note for people using union types where items can be strings or objects? E.g., `items: (string | {kind: 'image', url: string})[]` — recommend normalizing to objects with a `kind` field.

Jamie D: Yup. I'll add a short markdown section and two test prompt outputs for the eval harness. Also need someone to run link-checker on the new PR — I saw a few other docs PRs had broken anchors last week. @link-checker-bot can you do a pass on the branch? :pray:

link-checker-bot: Running link check on branch `docs/pr/482`... Found 1 broken anchor: `#structured-output-guidelines` referenced from docs/output.md.

Jamie D: Thanks — I'll fix the anchor and squash that into the PR.

Alex K: One more ask: include a one-liner in the API reference about parser behavior: "When returning top-level arrays, SDKs will automatically wrap them — prefer explicit envelopes to avoid ambiguity." Keep it short.

Priya R: LGTM. I'll do a quick pass for wording and examples after you push the edits. :thumbsup:

Jamie D: Plan: I'll update PR with the examples + anchor fix by EOD PST. If anyone wants to add alternative wording for the API reference line, drop it here and I'll pick one. Thanks folks. :rocket:
